  clock: 2  # d45e
  nonce: d45e  # d45e
  message: "RE-SIZED 2026-09-09, before any code was written. Instrument:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dodop_swift_09092026/shapes.py.\n\nTHIS ITEM'S HEADLINE NUMBER POOLS TWO POPULATIONS THAT ARE NOT THE SAME DEFECT,\nand one of them is not a defect at all. Re-measured on vapor at dev\n(4,944 external method-call edges; the filed 3,067 predates several swift PRs):\n\n    module slot FILLED with an external type      807   16.3%\n    type DERIVED but REFUSED (a PROJECT type)   1,305   26.4%   <- BY DESIGN\n    NO type derived at all                      2,832   57.3%   <- the real population\n\nswift.py refuses a project type in the module slot on purpose: \"A PROJECT type\nis a symbol, not a module; it rides in receiver_type_hint only\" (INV-kotob). It\nis right to, and it is exactly the guard objc is MISSING (WI-dason, filed today,\n583 of 3,300 objc slots name a first-party class). So the top refused types here\n-- Application 550, XCTApplicationTester 233, Request 165, URLEncodedFormDecoder\n42, Response 22 -- are the mechanism WORKING, not failing.\n\n**SO SWIFT DERIVES A RECEIVER TYPE FOR 42.7% OF THESE EDGES, NOT 16.5%.** The\nfiled figure understates the mechanism's reach by 26 points, and this item's real\ntarget is the 57.3% with no type at all -- still the largest single share, so the\nitem stands, but its size and its acceptance test both change. An acceptance test\nwritten against \"16.5% -> X%\" would be satisfied in part by routing project types\ninto the slot, which would be a REGRESSION.\n\nALSO REFUTED: this item's list of untyped callees (get 239, test 167, decode 85)\ncannot be reproduced from edge metadata, because **swift stamps no\nmeta[\"callee_name\"] at all** -- all 2,832 no-type edges carry None. The list must\nhave come from re-deriving the name from the dst id, which ADR-0036 ruling 1\nbans. That is WI-sabam's shape in a second language; recorded there.\n\nWHAT IS NOT YET KNOWN, and is the next step: which SOURCE SHAPES the 2,832\nuntyped receivers have. The classifier in shapes.py is written and correct but\nreturned zero, because it keyed sites on meta[\"callee_name\"] -- the field swift\ndoes not stamp. It needs re-keying on (file, line) plus the dst id's name\nsegment, and the symbol id's path is REPO-RELATIVE, not absolute.\n\nDIRECTION WARNING RESTATED, since it now applies to a smaller population: more\ntyped receivers feed section 7a sanitizer registration, and a registered barrier\nearns `sanitized` and DROPS the flow. Measure at L4 in both directions."  # d45e
- op: discuss  # 68a5
  at: '2026-09-10T03:51:08Z'  # 68a5
  by: agent  # 68a5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 68a5
  clock: 3  # 68a5
  nonce: 68a5  # 68a5
  message: "STAGE 1-3 MEASURED 2026-09-10, dev 33d3ea7116. This answers the \"WHAT IS NOT YET\nKNOWN\" step the re-sizing entry named. Record:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dodop_swift_09102026/ (PLAN.md pre-registered +\nADDENDUM 1; shapes2.py / untyped.py / props.py; RESULT.md).\n\nTHE PREVIOUS INSTRUMENT IS NOT RE-KEYED, IT IS REPLACED. dodop_swift_09092026/\nshapes.py matched sites by (line, callee_name) and swift stamps no callee_name.\nRe-keying it would still need a (line, name) join, and an edge carries a line but\nNOT a column, so a line with two calls cannot be attributed. The new probes drop\nthe join entirely: they enumerate call sites with the PRODUCTION parser and\nPRODUCTION `_extract_call_target`, and use the fact that the emit site stamps\n`gate_meta[\"receiver_type_hint\"]` whenever typing succeeds -- so its ABSENCE is\nexactly \"no type derived\". No id is parsed and no name is re-derived (ADR-0036 r1).\n\n*** THE MECHANISM, ON A MINIMAL PRODUCTION REPRO RATHER THAN A COUNT ***\n\n    db.write(2)        -> name='write' hint='db'   has_recv=True\n    self.db.write(1)   -> name='write' hint=None   has_recv=True\n    self.save()        -> name='save'  hint=None   has_recv=True\n\n`self` parses as `self_expression`, not `simple_identifier`. `_walk_nav` collects\nonly simple_identifiers into `receiver_parts`, so nothing lands there, and the\ninner `navigation_suffix` -- `db`, the token that IDENTIFIES the receiver -- is\nconsumed as `method_name` and then overwritten by the outer suffix. **WRITING\n`self.` IN FRONT OF A PROPERTY DESTROYS THE RECEIVER HINT FOR THE IDENTICAL\nCALL.** Corroborated from the other side: `B: hint 'self'` is 0 across 1,913\nclassified sites.\n\nThird language with this shape: objc WI-garar (self.<property> receiver never\ntyped); rust closed it as WI-dizag A.\n\n*** STAGE 2 -- THE UNTYPED POPULATION (vapor) ***\nReproduces the re-sizing exactly: 4,944 method edges, typed 2,112 (42.7%),\nuntyped 2,832 (57.3%). 1,913 classified, 525 on multi-call lines EXCLUDED and\ncounted, 21.5% dropped (pre-registered cap 25%).\n\n    938  49.0%  B: lowercase hint -- _type_of RAN and returned None\n    393  20.5%  A: self.<property>.<method>()\n    384  20.1%  A: self.<method>()\n    112   5.9%  A: chain off navigation_expression\n     86   4.5%  literals, call() result, tuples, super, ...\n\n**PRE-REGISTERED P4 REFUTED.** It predicted self-shaped receivers would be the\nlargest SINGLE bucket. They are 777 (40.6%) across two buckets; the largest\nsingle bucket is the 938 lowercase-hint sites where `_type_of` ran and failed.\nTwo comparable populations needing DIFFERENT fixes -- the same pooling this item\nwas re-sized for, one level down.\n\n*** STAGE 3 -- WHICH WOULD ACTUALLY FILL THE MODULE SLOT ***\nSite counts are not the deliverable: INV-kotob refuses a PROJECT type in the slot\non purpose, so typing a first-party receiver moves a site from \"no type\" to\n\"typed and rightly refused\" and reaches NO catalogue row (L5). Of the 393\nself.<property> sites: 233 (59.3%) external -> would fill the slot; 137 (34.9%)\nproject -> rightly refused; 23 (5.9%) undeclared. Top external receivers are real\nNIO/SwiftLog types: Logger 29, EventLoop 21, NIOLockedValueBox 52 across four\nnames, HTTPHeaders 11, EventLoopPromise 7, ByteBuffer 7.\n\n**THAT 59.3% IS AN ESTIMATE WITH A KNOWN BIAS AND NO ACCEPTANCE TEST MAY BE\nWRITTEN AGAINST IT.** props.py keys declarations by property NAME repo-wide, not\nby enclosing type, so a name used for two types resolves to whichever was seen\nfirst. Two artifacts are visible in its own output and are not hidden:\n`connection -> Name` is a collision, and `NIOLock` reads \"project\" though it is\nswift-nio's. The honest number comes from building the fix and measuring the\ndelta.\n\n*** WHERE THE FIX BELONGS -- READ, NOT ASSUMED ***\nNOT `_extract_call_target`, whose contract several passes depend on. The emit\ncascade already has a third stage (WI-higob slice 2):\n\n    if receiver_type is None and receiver_hint is None:\n        receiver_type = _swift_receiver_expr_type(\n            _swift_nav_receiver(node, source), source, ...)\n\n`_swift_nav_receiver` ALREADY hands it the `self.db` navigation_expression for\nthese sites, so `_swift_receiver_expr_type` is already called on them and already\nreturns None. The gap is INSIDE that helper -- narrow and already wired.\n`_inherited_field_type` is the existing per-enclosing-type resolver to reuse.\n\nNEXT: extend `_swift_receiver_expr_type` for the `self.<property>` head, measure\nat L4 in BOTH directions (a registered barrier DROPS a flow -- ADR-0052 recorded\nthat the escape-closing family's only reachable effect on findings today is\nsuppression), and price on PRIMITIVES REACHED, never on the typed-share percentage."  # 68a5
