- op: discuss  # d828
  at: '2026-09-10T04:34:31Z'  # d828
  by: agent  # d828
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d828
  clock: 5  # d828
  nonce: d828  # d828
  message: "SHIPPED 2026-09-10, PR #877, dev d638f50774. Measurement\ndocs/measurements/0028-swift-self-property-receiver.md.\n\n**STAYS OPEN, deliberately.** The self.<property> shape is fixed and measured;\nthe LARGER bucket -- 938 of 1,913 classified sites (49.0%) where `_type_of` RAN\nand returned None -- is untouched. Closing on this would read as \"swift receiver\ntyping is done\", which is false. Residuals filed as WI-* below so each is\nindependently trackable rather than living in this thread.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. `self` parses as `self_expression`, not `simple_identifier`, so\n`_walk_nav` collected nothing into `receiver_parts` and the inner\n`navigation_suffix` -- the token that IDENTIFIES the receiver -- was consumed as\na `method_name` and overwritten. Writing `self.` in front of a property destroyed\nthe hint for the identical call. Fixed in `_swift_receiver_expr_type` (where the\nWI-higob slice-2 cascade already routed these sites and returned None), NOT in\n`_extract_call_target`, and resolved through `_inherited_field_type` NOT\n`_type_of` -- the latter consults locals before fields, and a wrong stamp does\nnot merely fail to help: `method_call_recovery` step 3a treats a stamped\n`receiver_type_hint` as grounds to REFUTE a class hint, so it would DELETE a\ncorrect recovery. A shadowing-local test pins that.\n\nMODULE SLOT (the unit; NOT the typed share, which rises 368 where the slot rises\n252 because a PROJECT type is typed and then correctly refused per INV-kotob):\n\n    vapor        4,944 edges   807 -> 1,059   +252   0 lost\n    hummingbird  3,411 edges   654 ->   770   +116   0 lost\n    Kingfisher   2,504 edges   939 ->   987    +48   0 lost\n    Alamofire    3,233 edges   478 ->   504    +26   0 lost\n\n+442 total, 0 sites lost in any module in any repo, `method_edges` IDENTICAL\nacross arms (the internal control -- this re-keys slots and must not create an\nedge). Three of the four repos sized nothing. 25 of 25 sampled rows read back\nagainst source, 0 wrong-type.\n\nEND TO END (vapor, io-boundaries, cache-clear between arms): chains 43 -> 59,\ndistinct primitives 16 -> 17, 0 lost. **REPORTED AS \"+1 newly reachable primitive\n(NonBlockingFileIO.readChunked) and 2 substantive chains, plus 14 logging\nchains\", NOT as \"+16\"** -- 14 of the 16 land on `logging` and a severity-blind\nheadline would oversell it. Checking this mattered: measurement 0025 moved 787\ncorrect objc names and recall by ZERO.\n\n**PRE-REGISTERED P4 REFUTED.** It predicted self-shaped receivers would be the\nlargest SINGLE bucket. They are 777 (40.6%) across two; the largest is the 938\nwhere `_type_of` ran and failed.\n\nTWO INSTRUMENT ERRORS IN MY OWN OUTPUT, recorded in 0028 rather than quietly\nfixed: a `[:12]` truncation manufactured an `Array 20 -> 0` regression and an\n`EventLoop 0 -> 35` gain (caught by ARITHMETIC -- per-module deltas summed to\n+208 against a +252 total, so the breakdown could not be complete); and the\n\"59.3% external\" sizing figure keys declarations by property NAME repo-wide\n(`connection -> Name` is a visible collision in its own output), so it is an\nestimate with a known bias and is BARRED from being an acceptance criterion.\n\nOPEN QUESTION PUT TO THE OWNER, not decided here: WI-lafom moved AFNetworking\nprimitives 12->21 and net_recv 0->2; this cell moved 1 primitive and 2\nsubstantive chains for comparable build+measure cost. Whether a T0b cell counts\nas drained on \"correct, zero losses, verified rows\" or must show a substantive\nprimitive delta changes how much work the remaining seven cells represent."  # d828
