- op: discuss  # 1a31
  at: '2026-09-25T18:19:26Z'  # 1a31
  by: agent  # 1a31
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1a31
  clock: 7  # 1a31
  nonce: 1a31  # 1a31
  message: "DECISION 2026-09-25 (delegated by the owner in the P2 review follow-up: \"use a subagent to figure it out\"). CLOSED done under the owner's 2026-09-10 drain ruling (c), on the filed swift cell. Residuals are named below; two are new.\n\nTHE QUESTION AS POSED HERE (09-10, after PR #877): \"Whether a T0b cell counts as drained on 'correct, zero losses, verified rows' or must show a substantive primitive delta.\"\n\nIT WAS ALREADY ANSWERED, THE SAME DAY, ON THE PARENT, AND NEVER COPIED HERE. That is why the 09-25 P2 review saw it as pending. INV-linub, entry \"OWNER RULING 2026-09-10 -- WHAT DRAINS A CELL\":\n  (c) \"A CELL DRAINS ON CORRECTNESS. Right, zero losses, rows read back against source. No per-cell primitive delta is required. A SHIPPED, VERIFIED CELL NOW CLOSES ITS ROW HERE.\" The primitive demand moves to the ledger, to be shown ONCE over the drained set at T0c.\nFollow-through on the parent:\n- 09-11 \"T0b IS COMPLETE -- 10 OF 10 CELLS DRAINED\" lists \"swift WI-dodop #877\".\n- T0c (measurement 0029) inherited this cell's +1 primitive (NonBlockingFileIO.readChunked).\n- INV-linub was SATISFIED 09-11.\nEvery other cell on that roster is closed: INV-mumov, WI-garar, WI-sigog, WI-pokam, WI-vihop, WI-kikar, WI-dosuh, WI-kigub, WI-kafor, WI-lokun. This row was the only drained cell still open. No new criterion is needed. The decision is to APPLY (c) to this row.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, RE-RUN TODAY on dev 7821064366 (records: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dodop_ruling_09252026/):\n1. The #877 A/B instrument (dodop_swift_09102026/measure.py) on the same four repos. Output is IDENTICAL to #877's AFTER arm, including every per-module slot count. For vapor, the BEFORE arm read slot 807 and the AFTER arm 1,059, so the measurement discriminates, and the fix is live and unregressed:\n       vapor 4,944 edges  typed 2,480  SLOT 1,059\n       Alamofire 3,233    typed 1,303  SLOT   504\n       Kingfisher 2,504   typed 1,339  SLOT   987\n       hummingbird 3,411  typed 1,472  SLOT   770\n2. The filed shape through analyze_swift (fixture/Store.swift): `self.client.shutdown()` with `let client: HTTPClient` -> swift:HTTPClient:0-0:shutdown, hint=HTTPClient.\n3. The title's clause \"inferred and chained receivers NEVER reach the module slot\" is FALSE today, positively. On the same fixture, each of these reaches the HTTPClient slot:\n   - a constructor-inferred local (`let h = HTTPClient(...); h.shutdown()`)\n   - an annotated local\n   - a call result (`makeClient().shutdown()`)\n   - a local inferred from a call (`let h = makeClient(); h.shutdown()`)\n4. The title's \"only 16.5% (505/3,067)\": vapor today is 2,480/4,944 = 50.2% typed and 21.4% slot-filled. The 09-10 re-sizing already showed 16.5% pooled typed-and-rightly-refused project types (INV-kotob).\n\nTHE GENERAL CLAIM IS NOT ASSERTED. Swift receiver typing is not done. The re-run classifier (dodop_swift_09102026/untyped.py) finds vapor's untyped population now 2,464. Of 1,576 classified sites (24.8% dropped on multi-call lines, under the pre-registered 25% cap; 21.5% at #877), the residual rows are:\n    938  x.m(), _type_of returns None       -> WI-mofil (P2)\n    384  self.<method>()                    -> WI-sizas (P3)\n    112  a chain off a navigation_expression (includes self.a.b) -> WI-sizas (P3)\n     56  self.<property>.<method>() still untyped -> mostly collection / optional /\n         extension-declared properties, plus `any EventLoop` (7) -> WI-janad (NEW) for the `any` cause\n     86  literals, super, tuples, call() results -> not filed (no catalogue reach seen)\n\nNEW, FOUND WHILE VERIFYING, filed after a prior-art search (no hit):\n- WI-sulas (P2). A value chain `v.p.m()` is typed by its HEAD `v`: 1,020 sites on the 4 repos, 20 of 20 in a random sample wrong. 6 fill the slot with a wrong external type, and 14 stamp a wrong project hint, which method_call_recovery step 3a uses to REFUTE a class hint. The net_send overlay row Channel.addHandler matches 6 hummingbird sites ONLY through this error (addHandler belongs to ChannelPipeline). Fixing it loses them unless the row is re-keyed. This also means the \"typed\" share above overstates CORRECT typing: 572 of vapor's 2,480 typed are head-typed value chains.\n- WI-janad (P3). `name: any P` is not read as P. On a fixture, `any Channel` loses the catalogued Channel.writeAndFlush; 111 corpus sites (lower bound); 0 corpus catalogue reach verified.\n\nADR / RULE CLAUSES RELIED ON: the INV-linub owner ruling (c) of 2026-09-10; INV-kotob (a project type rides in the hint, never the slot); the closure-evidence discipline (a live repro on the production path plus the row's own instrument re-run); LIVE.md \"close on the filed row, file the residual\", and \"if the condition in the title still holds, done is false\" (both title clauses fail today, shown above).\n\nNOT VERIFIED: I did not re-run the #877 end-to-end io-boundaries A/B (chains 43 -> 59, +1 primitive). The slot maps are identical to #877's after arm, but I did not re-measure the primitive delta. The awaits_bakeoff_validation tag is left as it was."  # 1a31
